From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ios-blink-sideload <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:21:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: don't crash when UIAccessibility queries a dead
 view

-[RenderWidgetUIView accessibilityElements] dereferenced its weak
RenderWidgetHostViewIOS without checking it. UIAccessibility can still
query the UIView after a navigation has replaced and destroyed its
RenderWidgetHostViewIOS, and the weak pointer CHECK then aborts the app.
Anything that turns accessibility on (VoiceOver, Voice Control, UI
automation) hits it. Return no elements in that case, and when the page
has no accessibility root yet.

Status: verified at Chromium 4558926c in the iOS 27 simulator: loading a
failing URL with accessibility active crashed in this method before the
fix and no longer does.

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_ios_uiview.mm b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_ios_uiview.mm
index 122735282a3cf01f936a2943cc8432c66ad6009e..2762f2adf4f2041691117a64a0d731bce923ee40 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_ios_uiview.mm
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_view_ios_uiview.mm
@@ -1327,9 +1327,15 @@ - (nullable UITextRange*)characterRangeAtPoint:(CGPoint)point {
 }
 
 - (NSArray*)accessibilityElements {
+  // [ios-blink-sideload] UIAccessibility can still query this view after its
+  // RenderWidgetHostViewIOS is gone (e.g. right after a navigation swaps the
+  // view), and before the page's accessibility tree has a root.
+  if (!_view) {
+    return nil;
+  }
   ui::BrowserAccessibilityManager* manager =
       _view->host()->GetRootBrowserAccessibilityManager();
-  if (manager) {
+  if (manager && manager->GetBrowserAccessibilityRoot()) {
     id root =
         manager->GetBrowserAccessibilityRoot()->GetNativeViewAccessible().Get();
     if (root) {
